From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: cap SPI NOR frequency on ROCK Pi 4C

At spi-max-frequency = <108000000> the XT25F32B on ROCK Pi 4C returns
corrupt data on bulk reads: five reads of /dev/mtd0 give five different
checksums. At 10 MHz and 5 MHz reads are stable, but flashcp writes
fail verification at random offsets. At 1 MHz three flashcp writes of
the U-Boot SPI image verify clean. Cap the rate at 1 MHz.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4c.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4c.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4c.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4c.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-pi-4c.dts
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ &spi1 {
 	flash@0 {
 		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
 		reg = <0>;
-		spi-max-frequency = <108000000>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <1000000>;
 	};
 };
 
